{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0ee652287001d4ae33177d0b3def495535969f804b700a099122d4820b1cb305"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: direct tokio usage is forbidden; all async must go through the project's `runtime_async` asupersync wrapper, enforced by compile-time sealed traits, source grep guards, cargo-deny bans, and test-time checks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_90d4ae62b6f68a2efcf473f9a331a7a481ffd9adafe7c428d8d37bc2274ac33c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: releases must go exclusively through Doodlestein Self-Releaser (dsr) — doctor/health, quality, build, release, and verify commands — and GitHub Actions must never be inspected, triggered, or relied on for any claim."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d0137f85e3295818a0c7cb73a24b1869f1ff54f424ef2c9b638fd419f2146987"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: upstream WezTerm fixes are backported weekly via a read-only tracking ref with manual per-commit ports tagged `Upstream-WezTerm: <sha>`; blind pulls, merges, or bulk directory copies from upstream are prohibited."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ea459120c95ef373dc95284b07d23d0ea39ff717f607af8c2648befd82f69f66"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: agents may never delete files without explicit written permission, must not use git worktrees, must work on `main` (never `master`), and must avoid destructive commands like `git reset --hard` or `rm -rf` without explicit user authorization."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0ee652287001d4ae33177d0b3def495535969f804b700a099122d4820b1cb305","clm_90d4ae62b6f68a2efcf473f9a331a7a481ffd9adafe7c428d8d37bc2274ac33c","clm_d0137f85e3295818a0c7cb73a24b1869f1ff54f424ef2c9b638fd419f2146987","clm_ea459120c95ef373dc95284b07d23d0ea39ff717f607af8c2648befd82f69f66"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:07:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_801d643af87642f1850545957b1de1a1","id":"pg_7af27ee27d33575c8d63dfb4f7984352","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/dicklesworthstone-frankenterm-agents-md-9416f404da44-dfb4f7984352.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8994ddca19a95bc5984d678a5a61dc61"],"title":"Dicklesworthstone/frankenterm/AGENTS.md @ 9416f404da44","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:07:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_801d643af87642f1850545957b1de1a1"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_12c60edba7a308a82be3f81c29c71c2eb639390ea1e236841cf3a70b9fd5eff4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`ft` runs as the invoking user with no privilege separation; captured terminal bytes are redacted only on read surfaces, with the on-disk SQLite store holding raw bytes protected by file permissions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_735a327598ce7b0decf61d1f827a564edb2d08ccab93bbd6b104e417e8f48e20"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The threat model treats host compromise and pre-existing DB write access as out of scope (attacker-equivalent), and notes findings requiring those positions should be reported as normal bugs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dad1a5bf1de07d03a0856f07526352d88fca3e59476413bff9f3b0b3dda7959e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per its security policy, the project has no CVE pipeline (fixes tracked by bead and commit) and release artifacts are not yet signed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fb337e2cf51c4d55e0ea07500271d803daf8ee09719cd38d19a134f779f14511"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The stdio MCP transport (`ft mcp serve`) inherits the OS uid/gid with no in-band authentication, while MCP tool inputs are validated via workspace containment, size caps, and approval gating on mutating tools."}],"claim_ids":["clm_12c60edba7a308a82be3f81c29c71c2eb639390ea1e236841cf3a70b9fd5eff4","clm_735a327598ce7b0decf61d1f827a564edb2d08ccab93bbd6b104e417e8f48e20","clm_dad1a5bf1de07d03a0856f07526352d88fca3e59476413bff9f3b0b3dda7959e","clm_fb337e2cf51c4d55e0ea07500271d803daf8ee09719cd38d19a134f779f14511"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:07:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_801d643af87642f1850545957b1de1a1","id":"pg_967372f5d24054e1a61432dfa79308d6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/dicklesworthstone-frankenterm-security-md-9416f404da44-32dfa79308d6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_880d5122b7ad573b90f5c82a98faa882"],"title":"Dicklesworthstone/frankenterm/SECURITY.md @ 9416f404da44","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:07:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_801d643af87642f1850545957b1de1a1"}
